<article class="env-theorem" id="03VF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03VF">Theorem <span data-tag="03VF">64.27.2</span> <span class="named">(Grothendieck)</span>.</a>  Let $X$ be a connected scheme. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
There is a topology on $\pi _1(X, \overline{x})$ such that the open subgroups form a fundamental system of open nbhds of $e\in \pi _1(X, \overline x)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
With topology of (1) the group $\pi _1(X, \overline{x})$ is a profinite group. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The functor 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \begin{matrix}  \text{ schemes finite } \atop \text{ étale over }X 

&  \to 

&  \text{ finite discrete continuous } \atop \pi _1(X, \overline{x})\text{-sets}

\\  Y / X

&  \mapsto 

&  F_{\overline{x}}(Y) \text{ with its natural action} 

\end{matrix}  \]
</div>
<p>
 is an equivalence of categories. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      See <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/SGA1">SGA1</a>]</span>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>